1zvr|a|of Sustain ; Held up to a certain pitch, degree, or level; uniform; as, sustained pasion; a sustained style of writing; a sustained note in music.	j:fb0,68,3;1fon,63,4;dym,57,3;rvx,56,2;qgu,55,5;17uk,52,1;17uh,45,1;8ll,45,3;6hh,44,4;fd3,43,3;18ni,43,5;17xj,40,3;1hp7,39,8;5bv,36,3;1vdc,36,1~s81,26,9;1hp7,39,8;1le1,24,7;24cr,17,6;1eyh,5,5;o9q,22,5;236v,29,5;hnk,35,5;1psp,6,5;qgu,55,5;18ni,43,5;1wkt,6,4;1fon,63,4;15wz,10,4;1o59,15,4	e:16r8,14,4;16r0,9,6~16r0,9,6;16r8,14,4
